    "breadcrumb": "The GATAS Lab \u003e Projects",
    "content": "StructuredDecompositions.jl\nProject team Benjamin Merlin Bumpus Wilmer Leal Project articles Bumpus, B. M., Leal, W., Fairbanks, J., Karvonen, M., \u0026 Simard, F. (2026). Towards a Unified Theory of Time-Varying Data. Applied Categorical Structures, 34(3), 23. https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-026-09860-4 Azevedo, A. B., Bumpus, B. M., Capucci, M., Fairbanks, J., \u0026 Rosiak, D. (2025). Algorithmic and Extremal Obstructions Through the Language of Cohomology. arXiv. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2407.03488 Bumpus, B. M., Fairbanks, J., \u0026 Turner, W. J. (2024). Pushing Tree Decompositions Forward Along Graph Homomorphisms. arXiv. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2408.15184 Bumpus, B. M., Fairbanks, J., Genovese, F., Puca, C., \u0026 Rosiak, D. (2024). How nice is this functor? Two squares and some homology go a long way. Proceedings of Applied Category Theory, 2024. Bumpus, B. M., Capucci, M., Fairbanks, J., \u0026 Rosiak, D. (2024). Failures of compositionality: a short note on cohomology, sheafification and lavish presheaves. arXiv:2407.03488. Althaus, E., Bumpus, B. M., Fairbanks, J., \u0026 Rosiak, D. (2023). Compositional Algorithms on Compositional Data: Deciding Sheaves on Presheaves. arXiv. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2302.05575 Sponsors Computational sheaf theory has been supported by the DARPA program Automating Scientific Knowledge Extraction and Modeling.",
    "description": "StructuredDecompositions.jl\nProject team Benjamin Merlin Bumpus Wilmer Leal Project articles Bumpus, B. M., Leal, W., Fairbanks, J., Karvonen, M., \u0026 Simard, F. (2026). Towards a Unified Theory of Time-Varying Data. Applied Categorical Structures, 34(3), 23. https://doi.org/10.1007/s10485-026-09860-4 Azevedo, A. B., Bumpus, B. M., Capucci, M., Fairbanks, J., \u0026 Rosiak, D. (2025). Algorithmic and Extremal Obstructions Through the Language of Cohomology. arXiv. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2407.03488 Bumpus, B. M., Fairbanks, J., \u0026 Turner, W. J. (2024). Pushing Tree Decompositions Forward Along Graph Homomorphisms. arXiv. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2408.15184 Bumpus, B. M., Fairbanks, J., Genovese, F., Puca, C., \u0026 Rosiak, D. (2024). How nice is this functor? Two squares and some homology go a long way. Proceedings of Applied Category Theory, 2024. Bumpus, B. M., Capucci, M., Fairbanks, J., \u0026 Rosiak, D. (2024). Failures of compositionality: a short note on cohomology, sheafification and lavish presheaves. arXiv:2407.03488. Althaus, E., Bumpus, B. M., Fairbanks, J., \u0026 Rosiak, D. (2023). Compositional Algorithms on Compositional Data: Deciding Sheaves on Presheaves. arXiv. https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2302.05575 Sponsors Computational sheaf theory has been supported by the DARPA program Automating Scientific Knowledge Extraction and Modeling.",
