    "breadcrumb": "The GATAS Lab \u003e News",
    "content": "George Rauta presented Low-Mach Compressible Navier–Stokes Using Discrete Exterior Calculus on Rectilinear Grids at WCCM–ECCOMAS in Munich, with James Fairbanks and Liam Kunzendorf as co-authors.\nThe World Congress on Computational Mechanics and the ECCOMAS congress are where the computational mechanics community meets, which makes it a useful audience for the Decapodes work. The argument there is that writing a multiphysics model as a diagram of discrete exterior calculus operators is both cleaner to state and competitive to run.\nThe full list is on the talks page.",
    "description": "George Rauta presented Low-Mach Compressible Navier–Stokes Using Discrete Exterior Calculus on Rectilinear Grids at WCCM–ECCOMAS in Munich, with James Fairbanks and Liam Kunzendorf as co-authors.\nThe World Congress on Computational Mechanics and the ECCOMAS congress are where the computational mechanics community meets, which makes it a useful audience for the Decapodes work. The argument there is that writing a multiphysics model as a diagram of discrete exterior calculus operators is both cleaner to state and competitive to run.",
